# Line-ending policy for OMS-Frontend.
#
# Added 2026-08-26 while merging harshit, kamal, Mukesh and rathod-updates into
# `test`. Several branches were committing CRLF *into the blobs* while `test`
# held the same files as LF. Git compares blobs byte for byte, so every single
# line read as changed and merges degenerated into whole-file conflicts on top
# of a real diff of a few lines: src/services/ordersService.ts conflicted over
# all 703 lines to deliver 4 new ones, and src/pages/Add_Sales.tsx over all
# 4,290 to deliver 29. Both merged cleanly under `git merge -Xrenormalize`.
#
# `text=auto` makes git normalise to LF on check-in regardless of what the
# contributor's editor or core.autocrlf produced, so this cannot recur. Working
# copies on Windows are unaffected: core.autocrlf=true still checks files out
# with CRLF locally.
#
# Diagnosing a recurrence -- beware two false negatives seen while writing this:
#   * `git ls-files --eol` reports the *index/worktree* state and happily shows
#     `i/lf` for a file whose committed blob is CRLF.
#   * mingw awk and grep strip \r before matching, so `/\r$/` never fires.
# What actually works:
#   git show <ref>:<path> | tr -cd '\r' | wc -c        # non-zero => CRLF blob
#   git diff --numstat --ignore-cr-at-eol A B -- <path> # the real change size

* text=auto

*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.scss  text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.xlsx  binary
